   "method": "Flammability threshold testing in quiescent environments was conducted following NASA STD 6001 Test 1 procedures.",
   "test": "The method is an upward flame propagation test in a quiescent environment using a well-defined igniter flame at the bottom of a vertically mounted sample.",
   "pass": "A material passes this test if the vertical burn length is less than 15.2 cm and there is no evidence of transfer of burning debris",
   "moc": "The MOC was the oxygen concentration where at least three samples passed the NASA-STD-6001 burning criteria of less than 15.2 cm burn length",
   "below": "The materials reported with ULOIs and MOCs less than 30 burned at least 15.2 cm in 30 % oxygen, while the materials reported with ULOIs and MOCs larger than 40 burned less than 15.2 cm in 40 % oxygen.",
